# Home-image content lives in the chezmoi source home/ (attribute-encoded names:
# dot_*, private_*, executable_*, symlink_*). Ignore runtime state and per-host
# scratch, but keep the placeholder keep.me files so empty dirs survive.
home/private_dot_ssh/hosts/*
home/private_dot_ssh/sockets/*
!home/private_dot_ssh/hosts/private_empty_keep.me
!home/private_dot_ssh/sockets/private_keep.me
home/dot_vimbackup/*
home/dot_config/zed/settings_backup.json
# Runtime dirs must never enter the chezmoi source:
home/dot_local/share/
home/dot_local/apps/

# Repo-root artifacts: agent/vibe-palace state. Never tracked, never stowed
# (they sit outside the home/ package, so stow cannot see them). These live in
# the vibe-palace vault (Projects/dotfiles/), never in this repo.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/commit.msg
/resume.md
/iterations.md
/tasks/
/.claude/
/.grok/
/.vibe-palace/

# vibe-palace also drops per-session claim markers (.vibe-palace/claimed-*) in
# whatever directory a command runs from — which can land INSIDE the home/ source
# tree (e.g. home/dot_local/bin/fetch.bins/.vibe-palace/), where a committed copy
# would be replicated onto every machine by `chezmoi apply`. The anchored rule
# above only covers repo root, so ignore .vibe-palace/ at ANY depth as well.
.vibe-palace/
